comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T11:09:40.162Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented in PR 1752. runExtensionExploreManageAction calls prepareExploreManageState(ctx, settings), which runs readAndAdoptExploreManageState (read managed state, list installed packages, adopt unmanaged ones) under withExtensionInstallLock only when manage adopts (--fix-managed-state). refreshManagedExtensionUpdates then runs after the lock is released. requiresExtensionStateLock no longer wraps manage --fix-managed-state at dispatch; doctor --fix-managed-state is unchanged. Nothing after adoption writes state: the second inventory listing, the runtime probe and triage only read. Test: tests/integration/extensions/manage-lock-scope.integration.spec.ts runs manage --fix-managed-state with a stalled npm on PATH, waits until the lookup has started, and acquires the scope lock with a single attempt, which succeeds. Negative control: moving the refresh back inside the lock makes that acquisition fail.\n"
